# Dashboard presentation and interaction contracts

Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/referencia/dashboard-ux.md` (DUX-01..09),
`docs/referencia/dashboard.md` and the active approved scope. These are current
operator decisions for the local Dashboard. Archived Phase 26/28 plans retain
history; they do not restore superseded UI. Apply the affected contracts without
expanding unrelated work. Codex authors policy; implementation follows it.

- DUX-01: prioritize graphs and useful human values. Overview state/workload
  charts each use full width. Counters are secondary, small, gray and normal
  weight (`40/40 loaded` for the map). Axes remain legible without technical
  captions or overlapping ticks.
- DUX-02: explanations/definitions/provenance live behind an italic circled `i`
  using `InformationControl`, with a contextual accessible name, keyboard/modal
  focus, Escape and scroll-free focus return. Meaningful errors/partial coverage
  remain visible.
- DUX-03: no wall of run/sequence cards. No selection means no run detail; one
  exact selection owns one timeline. Run metadata/lineage goes in information;
  attempt/day lists are closed disclosures by default. Use the same human
  ordinal/iteration/role caption in attempt graph, controls and modal.
- DUX-04: use authoritative short names, max 35 trimmed Unicode code points for
  new preparer input. IDs remain internal selection/lineage keys, absent from
  graph tooltips, and last when shown in inspection metadata. Never merge
  duplicate aliases, infer roles from names or rewrite frozen inputs to rename.
- DUX-05: preserve page position through selection, refresh and loading; no
  chart-triggered scrollIntoView. Map viewport is at most 500 px with internal
  two-axis scrolling. Reserve calendar geometry while changing metrics. Separate
  filter/action rows. Keep escaped tooltips inside the viewport and below modals.
- DUX-06: project/preset applies immediately; coherent valid typed scope applies
  after 400 ms, without Apply. Invalid drafts retain the prior valid scope. Fence
  late replies and retire sensitive content on scope/selection changes. Preserve
  Pause/visibility, at most 2 active reads, adaptive batches up to 1000 rows and
  honest progress.
- DUX-07/08: reuse time.ts for selected-IANA `DD/MM/yyyy HH:mm`, day
  `DD/MM/yyyy`, compact contextual axis ticks and `XX h XX m` durations. Positive
  sub-minute values use `<1 m`; unknown stays unavailable. Preserve raw API time,
  named-zone day buckets and metric math; never rewrite inspected content bytes.
- DUX-09: use proportionate evidence from production components/callers. Scroll
  and delayed-response regressions need real browser geometry, not only a
  screenshot or unit mock. Governance-only edits need links/consistency/docs,
  not runtime tests matching wording.

`ai_dev_loop` owns mutable presentation metadata separately from frozen inputs.
Read-only Dashboard paths never migrate or rename data. Shared API/HTTP bounds,
role-aware exact-ID content reads, generation fencing and loopback security stay
in force. No installation, timer change, real ledger mutation, model turn, Git
publication or final acceptance follows from these UI rules.
